# Architecture Decisions

## Content Management Strategy
- No CMS (Sanity) is integrated yet. All content is hardcoded or in static files.
- Sanity can be added later incrementally (page by page, on a branch) without downtime or rewriting existing components.
- If a CMS is added, work on a separate branch, test via Vercel preview URLs, and deploy when ready.
- The current component/layout/auth/Stripe work is NOT wasted — a CMS only changes where text comes from, not the templates.

## Document Storage
- Admin-swappable documents live in Supabase Storage bucket "documents" (toolbox, nhg, other-studies, facilitator, lessons, questions, kf-resources).
- Use `docUrl()` from `src/lib/storage-url.ts` to convert static `/docs/...` paths to Supabase Storage public URLs.
- The admin panel Documents tab manages these files (upload, replace, delete).

## Admin Panel
- Located at `src/app/(member)/admin/` under the member layout.
- Protected by `ADMIN_ONLY_ROUTES` in `src/proxy.ts` — only `tier === "admin"` users can access.
- Members tab: search, filter, upgrade/downgrade tiers, activate/suspend.
- Documents tab: browse by category, upload, delete via Supabase Storage API.
- API routes at `/api/admin/update-member` and `/api/admin/documents` use the service role key.

## Tier Enforcement
- `src/proxy.ts` enforces three route groups: `MEMBER_ROUTES`, `KF_ONLY_ROUTES`, `ADMIN_ONLY_ROUTES`.
- Missing profile or inactive user → redirect to `/login`.
- NHG users on KF-only routes → redirect to `/nhg`.
- Non-admin users on admin routes → redirect to their home page.

## Email
- Contact form sends via Resend (`/api/contact`).
- Automated emails (matching KF date sheet) can use Vercel Cron + Supabase for templates + Resend — no CMS needed.

## Future: Announcements
- If the admin needs to post banners/announcements without code changes, add an `announcements` table in Supabase and a new admin tab. This is Option 1 (lightweight, no CMS).
- Option 2 (editable content blocks) or Option 3 (full Sanity CMS) can be layered on later.
